{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_twym7gggx2impgiyjoezq4jywhr4myh3xlw5q5wpu76prrfzy72q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 4 tests pass. The implementation is complete:\n\n- **`Mdb::create`** — writes a text superblock (db_name, key_size_max, data_size_max, hash_buckets, items_max), initializes the index file with a free-list pointer plus zeroed bucket pointers, and creates an empty data file.\n- **`Mdb::open`** — re-reads the superblock by parsing whitespace-separated tokens and opens index/data files in read-write mode.\n- **`read` / `write` / `delete`** — walk the bucket's chain by comparing keys (treating the first NUL as a terminator, matching C's `strcmp`), with the C semantics for inserting new entries, updating existing ones (free old data, allocate/write new), and unlinking on delete.\n- **`hash`** — `sum(byte * index)` with wrapping arithmetic to match the C implementation.\n- **`data_alloc`** — scans the data file for a contiguous run of zero bytes large enough for `size + 2`, returning `start + 1` (preserving the C padding semantics); falls back to appending zero bytes at end-of-file.\n- **`index_alloc` / `index_free`** — manage the embedded free-list at offset 0 of the index file exactly as in C.\n- **`read_index` / `write_index`** — read/write the on-disk layout (`next_ptr`, key buffer of `key_size_max` bytes, `value_ptr`, `value_size`) using little-endian byte conversions.\n\nAll four port tests (`happy_test0`, `reopen_test1`, `load_test2`, `load_test3`) pass."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":820,"cache_read_input_tokens":58339,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":820,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64697785-163b-4426-ac3a-bb677c00c64a","uuid":"0a20d33b-4cc8-4730-9399-10505